#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:21
msgid "What is Gadly?"
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:22
msgid ""
"Gadly is a collection of free online utilities for text editing, social "
"media, finance, web/SEO, file management, and more. All tools run in your "
"browser—no installation required."
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:25
msgid "Is my data safe?"
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:26
msgid ""
"Most tools process data locally in your browser or send it only for the "
"specific operation (e.g., translation, meta tag check). We do not store or "
"log your personal data. For sensitive content, always check the privacy "
"policy."
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:29
msgid "Does it work on mobile?"
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:30
msgid ""
"Yes! The site is responsive and optimized for smartphones and tablets. You "
"can use all tools from your mobile device."
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:33
msgid "Are Gadly tools free?"
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:34
msgid ""
"Yes. The utilities on this site are free for typical personal and work use. "
"Technical limits (such as maximum file size) depend on the specific tool and "
"are shown when relevant."
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:39
msgid "Account and Access"
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:41
msgid "Do I need an account to use Gadly?"
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:42
msgid ""
"No. Most tools are available immediately without registration. If a tool or "
"feature requires login, you will see a clear message before continuing."
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:45
msgid "I forgot my password. What can I do?"
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:46
msgid ""
"Use the password reset option on the login page. If your email is verified, "
"you can reset your password and access your account again."
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:49
msgid "Can I change my username or profile image?"
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:50
msgid ""
"Yes. Open your account profile from the header menu and update your "
"username, email, and avatar from there."
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:55
msgid "Usage and Results"
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:57
msgid "Why is a result different from another website?"
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:58
msgid ""
"Some tools use different rules, formulas, or rounding methods depending on "
"implementation. If you need strict precision (for legal or accounting use), "
"always verify with your official reference."
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:61
msgid "Why does a tool return an error with a URL?"
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:62
msgid ""
"The URL may be blocked, invalid, or unavailable from the server side. Check "
"that it starts with http/https, that the page is public, and that the domain "
"is reachable."
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:65
msgid "Can I use these tools for work or clients?"
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:66
msgid ""
"Yes, but always review the output before publishing or delivering it. Gadly "
"helps speed up work, but final validation is your responsibility."
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:71
msgid "Site and preferences"
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:73
msgid "Can I use dark mode or a warm color theme?"
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:74
msgid ""
"Yes. Use the theme and warm-tone controls in the site header. Your choices "
"are saved in the browser so the look stays the same on your next visit."
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:77
msgid "What does the cookie banner do?"
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:79
#, python-format
msgid ""
"It remembers that you have read the notice so we do not show it on every "
"page load. We use minimal cookies and local storage for preferences as "
"described in the <a href=\"%(privacy_url)s\">Privacy Policy</a>."
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:82
msgid "How do I change language or save favorite tools?"
msgstr ""

#: .\tools\templates\tools\faq.html:83
msgid ""
"Use the language control in the header where translations are available. If "
"you are logged in, you can star tools on the home page to keep them handy in "
